<<~ ahu slot=`#/placement-measurement-completed-inventory`>>

! Placement measurement — completed inventory

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/disk-ingress-boundary`>>

!! Disk ingress boundary

The boundary does not yet bind the source mirror to its destination. `lares-cli/src/commands/ingest.ts` accepts `--source` and `--to` independently; `ingest-core.ts:fileToUriForSource` explicitly leaves designation of the target to the caller. The island's `action-handler.ts` writes through `access.write(action.toBag)` and does not authenticate the source path against a mirror grant. LOAD similarly accepts supplied carriers and `toBag`, with `sourceUri` as provenance. A structural ward must bind a disk wave to an actual granted mirror and its bag at a trusted boundary, including deletions, renames and kāpae. It must account for deliberate LOAD from arbitrary source directories into a working layer.

Foreign titles are legitimate content: native packs and the kahua title-path mirror preserve titles independently of the resting bag. The `bag` field must not select the store; the selected store does. A title-prefix check would violate the ruling. Observe sources already refuse at the CLI, but that check alone does not establish the destination grant at the island.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/current-homes-and-readers`>>

