| Mailbox, delegate, face-row, lease-epoch, other ledger | node `vessel-mailbox.ts`, tw5 `daemon-vm-core.ts`, mesh `epoch-lease.ts` | daemon-associated stores; exact per-writer layer requires further tracing |

!!! Completed trace of the remaining families

| Family | Writers and readers | Current rest |h
| Mailbox | `node/vessel-mailbox.ts` parks and marks delivered via explicit `composite.put(..., {bag: DAEMON_BAG_ID})`; drain lists and reads from the composite. Node vessel wiring parks undeliverable alerts and drains on wiki breath. Browser wiring warns and drops. | daemon document |
| Delegate / face-row | `tw5/daemon-vm-core.ts` builds request data in memory and calls `runLocalVerb`; `verb-local-dispatch.ts` invokes the registered handler. Face-row responses return over the socket. These are not persisted invocation records. | no row; handler business effects land according to that handler |
| Lease epoch | `node/lease-rekey.ts` writes to a supplied handle; persona lease and vessel rekey pass the daemon handle. Vessel readers scan that same daemon document (`open-node-vessel.ts`, `vessel-raise.ts`). | daemon document |
| Swarm | Signed acts write through `node/commands/swarm.ts` to the face's promote-board document; readers fold that board. Separate transient `$:/lares/swarm/**` UI rows live in the daemon wiki. | face promote board for signed acts; daemon wiki layers for UI controls |
| Ward audit | `tw5/worker-data-verbs.ts` calls bagless `composite.put`, which routes to default writable. Tests and handler behavior place it in the wiki working layer. | wiki working layer |
| Persona acts | Founding writes genesis acts to the persona plane (`keyhive/ceremony-core.ts`); device admit appends there (`node/persona-act-store.ts` from `commands/device-admit.ts`). Admission also copies carried acts to the local daemon document (`ceremony-core.ts`), creating a duplicate. Boot proof and several readers fold persona + daemon docs; lease, swarm, promote, intent and kahua readers generally read persona plane only. | persona plane plus redundant local daemon copy |

The per-family guards/readers include `node/tests/uds-face-row-socket-only.test.ts`, `tw5/tests/daemon-vm-run-as-face.test.ts`, `node/tests/lease-rekey.test.ts`, `raise-reads-the-leased-epoch.test.ts`, `mesh/tests/swarm-board.test.ts`, `swarm-door.test.ts`, `tw5/tests/worker-data-verbs.test.ts`, `node/tests/persona-act-boot.test.ts`, `mesh/tests/persona-act-board.test.ts`, `keyhive/tests/shared-face-docs.test.ts`, and `node/tests/device-admit-face-edge.test.ts`. Mailbox lacks a named node test; `tw5/tests/seal-refusal-reaches-the-ledger.test.ts` covers related wiring.

The family count corrects two earlier overgeneralizations: delegate and face-row invocation rows do not persist, and signed swarm acts sit on a face promote board rather than in the daemon wiki. The daemon wiki's swarm UI remains a distinct family.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/homes-to-mint`>>

!! Homes to mint

`wiki-recipe.ts:expandRecipe` currently derives canon from the wiki slug; `daemon-vm-core.ts` adds the daemon document and optionally persona document to its composite and builds the daemon recipe through `kahuaRecipe`. The working document receives outcomes and receipts independently of the daemon document. A control home therefore needs an explicit vessel-scoped document and handle, write routing for all control writers, and reader subscriptions; merely renaming the daemon bag cannot move the working-slot records or per-bag effects.

A secret home needs separate document custody and access grants, never a wiki recipe layer or a disk mirror. Founding and admission (`keyhive/src/ceremony-core.ts`, `node/src/commands/init.ts`, `commands/device-admit.ts`), replay, peer sync and browser construction must all follow it. Persona acts currently occupy more than one document, so every owner and reader needs an explicit sweep. Face-bound daemon canon needs minting at face creation/join, registry and capability binding, recipe expansion and a per-face mirror (`node/src/bag-paths.ts`); `bags/kahua` remains the read-only next library.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/predicate-candidates`>>

!! Predicate candidates

The residency uses of `isControlPlaneUri`, `isDaemonCanonWithheld`, `isBagManifestUri`, `isVolatileVmUri`, `isEffectRecordUri`, `isRealmBagAnnounceUri`, `isNexusHandlesUri`, `isTempLayerInternalTitle`, `declaresNoProjection`, and the residency runs in `projection-filter.ts` need review. Some helpers also serve non-projection semantics: for example, effect-record retirement and enumeration use `isEffectRecordUri` in `composite-store.ts`; removing those uses without replacing their actual ledger contract would change behavior. `isVolatileVmUri` also routes VM scratch in `island-adaptor.ts`. Ownership, identity and routing uses need separate treatment from residency decisions.

Inventory completed for the families named by the ruling. Delegate and face-row invocation requests do not persist; signed swarm acts remain on the face promote board, while transient swarm UI controls rest in daemon wiki layers. Step 3 must preserve these distinctions while moving the persisted daemon control families. The mirror-source grant gap remains the structural dependency Step 4 must close.

<<~/ahu>>

